What are Locators?

A locator is simply a way to tell Playwright:
"Hey, find this element on the page."
For example:
Search box
Login button
Username field
Product name
All these are elements, and locators help us identify them.


1. getByRole() ⭐ Recommended
Finds elements using their accessibility role and visible name.
HTML
<button>Login</button>
TypeScript
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Login' }).click();

Why Playwright recommends it?
Because it behaves like a real user.

A user sees:
Login button
not
button with id="btn123"


Common Roles: 
Element                       Role
button                      button
input                   	textbox
checkbox                	checkbox
radio button            	radio
link	                    link
dropdown                	combobox

Example
await page.getByRole('textbox').fill('Kirti');
HTML:
<input type="text">



2. getByText()
Finds elements using visible text.

HTML
<h1>Welcome Kirti</h1>
TypeScript
await page.getByText('Welcome Kirti').click();

Example:
HTML
<button>Submit</button>

TypeScript
await page.getByText('Submit').click();


Verification Example
await expect(
  page.getByText('Login Successful')
).toBeVisible();


3. CSS Selectors using locator()
In Playwright, CSS selectors are generally used through locator().

a. By ID

HTML
<input id="username">
TypeScript
await page.locator('#username').fill('Kirti');
# means ID.

b. By Class

HTML
<button class="login-btn">
TypeScript
await page.locator('.login-btn').click();
. means class.

c. By Attribute

HTML
<input placeholder="Enter Email">
TypeScript
await page
  .locator('[placeholder="Enter Email"]')
  .fill('kirti@gmail.com');


d. By Tag Name

HTML
<button>Login</button>
TypeScript
await page.locator('button').click();



Comparison

HTML
<button id="buy-btn">
  Buy Now
</button>
Using getByRole()
await page.getByRole('button', {
  name: 'Buy Now'
}).click();

Using getByText()
await page.getByText('Buy Now').click();

Using CSS Selector
await page.locator('#buy-btn').click();


Which One Should You Prefer?
1️⃣ getByRole()
page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Login' })
Most reliable and recommended.

2️⃣ getByText()
page.getByText('Submit')
Good when text is unique.

3️⃣ locator() with CSS
page.locator('#login-btn')
Use when role/text is unavailable or unstable.


getByRole()  (Highest Priority)
      ↓
getByText()
      ↓
locator(CSS) (Lower Priority)


Why?

getByRole(): 
User-centric
Accessibility-friendly
More stable
Playwright recommended


getByText()
Good, but text change ho sakta hai.

CSS Selector
IDs/classes frequently change ho sakte hain.
Maintenance zyada hoti hai.

I prefer getByRole() first because Playwright recommends user-facing locators. If role-based identification is not feasible, I use getByText(). CSS selectors via locator() are generally my fallback option."